"""Build the shareable GC500 asset map — one self-contained HTML file.

Usage: python print/build_asset_app.py

Everything the page needs is embedded: the asset register, the drawing sheets as images, and the callout
coordinates. It opens from a file, works with no network, no login and no server, and can be emailed or dropped in
a folder. Records added in the page are saved in that browser only and exported as JSON — the page says so, and it
is not a shared database.

Pricing: no rates have been supplied. The rate fields are empty and every total reads 'no rate supplied' until
someone types a rate in. Nothing is estimated.

Output: print/out/GC500_Delivery_Control.html
"""
from __future__ import annotations
