# Two kinds of picture, and the page must never let them blur into each other.
#
#   'photo' \u2014 a PHOTOGRAPH Andrew Fisher supplied on 11 Sep 2026. A real Coates unit, camera, daylight. It still
#            stands for the product rather than for the particular one delivered, and the card says so.
#   'made'  \u2014 a MADE PICTURE. Nobody photographed this; it was generated to show what the product looks like,
#            because the register had 19 lighting towers, 15 barriers and 11 generators showing an empty box.
#            It is accurate enough to recognise a machine on a gate and it is not evidence of anything. The card
#            labels it, in orange, in words, and the caption says it in full.
#
# The distinction is not decoration. A drop photograph, a product photograph and a made picture are three
# different claims about the world, and this page has to be readable by a driver who has never met any of us.
