  /* v5.79 — A SILENT TOMBSTONE, so the typo cannot come back. v5.76 wrote none, on the ground that a typo was
     never there; but a number typed on one phone reaches the other copies at the next sync, and a copy that
     still carries it hands it straight back at the merge after that — the very hole the 14 Sep 2026 audit
     found (TR-01), reopened for typed numbers. So the erase leaves a tombstone after all, marked as an erase,
     and every page treats it as silence: the drawer shows nothing, offers nothing, and the Journal writes no
     line for it (a typo is not an event on the job). It exists only so that no copy of the record can put the
