   re-pointing what was recorded or renaming the reference, he chose MOVE (17 Sep 2026) — a reference is never
   renamed, because the schedule's rows, the drawing's callouts and the rental system's lines all hang off it.

   What moves is what people RECORDED against the reference — the light and its history, the ticks, what turned
   up (the supplied record and its numbers), the numbers typed, the things inside, the accessories added here, the
   note, the branch, the Rental ID, the weeks and the hire start. What stays is the schedule's own (what it asked
   for, where it goes, the numbers it allocated), the photographs of the place, the map attached to the place, and
   every record with an id of its own (a variance, a breakdown, a cost, an action) — those carry a reference box
   in their own dialog. The move refuses a target that already carries a record, and says what it carries.

   The move is written down, not done by stealth: `moves[from] = {to, at, by}` and a line in the history of the
   light. Every reader of the source asks movedAway() first and reads nothing recorded there, local or committed,
