   is, the words the schedule used, and the row those words came off. An accessory added on the page carries the
   moment it was added instead of a row, which is unique to it. Two identical entries on one reference — two
   chairs off the same row, written the same way — would collide, so the second and later ones carry their turn
   in the list; the build's order is the schedule's order and does not shuffle between rebuilds.

