   being prevented. The build now carries the committed removals (COMMITTED.deleted) and this folds the two.

   The fold is the rule the merge already uses, not a new one: take the LATER removal across both records and
   the LATER putting-back across both, and whichever of those two is later stands. A tie stands as removed — a
   thing that should not be there is worse on a drop sheet than a thing missing from one. So a removal typed on
