   ticked building, not a rate times the row's quantity. The two agree exactly while every building is ticked
   the same way — WC15 with both toilet blocks levelled is 2 × $104.10 either way — so nothing anybody has
   already recorded moves. They part only when a person says one building was levelled and the other was not,
   which is the whole reason for the change.

   A ticked line the card cannot price (`absent`, `poa`, `spread`) is counted as work recorded and money
   UNKNOWN: the total is blocked rather than quietly short, because a charge nobody can price is not nought. */
function labourMoney(ref, l, key, asset){
  const a = asset || allAssets().find(x => x.key === ref);
  const units = a ? labourUnits(a) : [];
  const qty = qtyOf(l);
  if (!units.length) {
